Independent policy-review date: 2026-07-19
Result: BLOCKED

Implementation commit `023ea6ca6858141a8c66bbe9e02c2b65bf4c1483` passed the
main and clean-checkout matrices with 64 tests and pre-commit. Independent review
then found a HIGH safety blocker before acceptance:

- `make db-reset` is allowlisted by `.codex/hooks/enforce_docker_boundary.py`.
- The Make recipe runs `docker compose --profile dev down -v`.
- `.codex/rules/default.rules` only prompts for the different prefix order
  `docker compose down -v`, and the rule engine cannot inspect a Make recipe.
- The allowlisted target can therefore remove local PostgreSQL volumes without
  the intended destructive-action prompt.

